# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, correct.
#
# Without this file every `docker build` uploads the whole working tree —
# including local node_modules and every package's dist/. That is slow, and it
# is also a correctness problem: the Dockerfiles run `pnpm install` themselves,
# and a host node_modules copied in first can shadow it with binaries built for
# the wrong platform. The resulting failure is a native module crashing at
# runtime, which points nowhere near the real cause.

# Dependencies — installed inside the image, never copied in.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# Build output — produced inside the image.
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
*.tsbuildinfo
.vite
**/.vite

# Version control and CI.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Secrets. Belt and braces: .env is gitignored, but a build context is taken
# from the working tree, not from git, so an untracked .env would otherwise be
# copied straight into an image layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Test and tooling artefacts that no image needs.
coverage
**/coverage
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
test-results
**/test-results
**/screenshots
e2e
**/e2e

# Agent tooling and docs — not part of any runtime.
.claude
docs
deploy
*.md
!README.md

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.log
